WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.025
Context is the token sequence available to the model for the current request.

00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:07.920
It includes instructions, conversation, documents, code, tool output,

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.040
and generated history.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.560
Longer context increases cache memory and prompt-processing time.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.150
Short chat and rewriting usually need modest context.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.160
Long-document analysis and summarization may need more,

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.285
but retrieval or chunking can be more reliable than placing an entire archive into one

00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:22.800
prompt.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.530
Coding workloads vary from a small function to repository-wide analysis.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.710
Useful context depends on file selection, language, tools,

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.080
and the model's ability to use distant information.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.100
Maximum context does not guarantee maximum understanding.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.850
Retrieval-augmented generation adds selected source passages to a prompt.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.095
Its workload includes embeddings, indexing, retrieval quality, context assembly,

00:00:43.095 --> 00:00:43.920
and citations.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.840
Agents add tool calls, state, repeated prompts, and potentially long histories.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.605
Vision-language models add image encoding, visual tokens, adapters,

00:00:51.605 --> 00:00:52.950
and image-memory requirements.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.640
Batch processing and multiple users multiply cache and compute demand.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.840
The same base model can behave very differently across these workloads.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.570
Size context for the actual application and cap unnecessary history.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.566
Measure prompt-processing latency, cache growth, accuracy, and failure behavior.

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:11.920
A smaller context used with disciplined information selection often outperforms an

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.183
oversized noisy prompt.

00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:17.345
Define a workload envelope with typical and worst-case prompt length, output length,

00:01:17.345 --> 00:01:19.700
images, tools, sessions, and request rate.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.840
Capacity planning needs that envelope, not one carefully chosen demonstration prompt.
